      "message": "in other TCPCs, when using CONFIG_USB_PD_VBUS_DETECT_TCPC we do the following sequence:\n        usb_charger_vbus_change(port, tcpc_vbus[port]);\n        task_wake(PD_PORT_TO_TASK_ID(port));\n(see in tcpci_tcpc_alert() in driver/tcpm/tcpci.c)\n\nwhere usb_charger_vbus_change() is implemented in common/usb_charger.c as :\n        /* If VBUS has transitioned low, notify PD module directly */\n        if (!vbus_level)\n                pd_vbus_low(port);\n        /* Update VBUS supplier and signal VBUS change to USB_CHG task *                \n        charge.voltage \u003d USB_CHARGER_VOLTAGE_MV;\n        charge.current \u003d vbus_level ? USB_CHARGER_MIN_CURR_MA : 0;\n        charge_manager_update_charge(CHARGE_SUPPLIER_VBUS,\n                                             port,\n                                             \u0026charge);\n        /* USB Charger task(s) */\n        task_set_event(USB_CHG_PORT_TO_TASK_ID(port), USB_CHG_EVENT_VBUS, 0);\n\nSo at least, the pd_vbus_low() is never done here ?\nI don\u0027t know either why you would not need the charge supplier.",
